IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc4-carers-allowance`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), Part V, disablement pension, increases, successive accidents, prescribed diseases, ss 103-110 (ss 102 and 111 are shown blank in this text).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Plain-text rendering by a converter script, not the official text.
-- BAR POLARITY: a "shall not be entitled" function answers "is the person barred?": JUST TRUE = the text says not entitled; JUST FALSE = the text says no bar (a failed "if", an "unless" met, an exception); NOTHING = silent.
-- GRANT POLARITY: a grant with "if" gives JUST FALSE when a limb of the "if" fails; a grant with only "where" gives NOTHING (fork F7).
-- Schedule 4 amounts (table omitted from this text) and Schedule 6 assessments are inputs, named as the plan names them.

§ `Part V -- Benefit for industrial injuries: disablement and prescribed diseases`

§§ `s 103 -- Disablement pension`

-- s 103(1): "Subject to the provisions of this section, an employed earner shall be entitled to disablement pension if he suffers as the result of the relevant accident from loss of physical or mental faculty such that the assessed extent of the resulting disablement amounts to not less than 14 per cent. or, on a claim made before 1st October 1986, 20 per cent."
-- The bar in subsection (6) and the rounding and aggregation in (2) to (4) are other functions; the seat layer puts them together.
-- src:2347 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this section, an employed earner shall be entitled to disablement pension if he suffers as the result of the relevant accident from loss of physical or mental faculty such that the assessed extent of the resulting disablement amounts to not less than 14 per cent. or, on a claim made before 1st October 1986, 20 per cent.
@ref s 103(1) (src:2347)
GIVEN date IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 103(1) the least extent of disablement for a claim made on the date, as a percentage` MEANS
    IF   date LESS THAN Date 1 10 1986
    THEN 20    -- "on a claim made before 1st October 1986, 20 per cent."
    ELSE 14    -- "not less than 14 per cent."

-- src:2347 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this section, an employed earner shall be entitled to disablement pension if he suffers as the result of the relevant accident from loss of physical or mental faculty such that the assessed extent of the resulting disablement amounts to not less than 14 per cent. or, on a claim made before 1st October 1986, 20 per cent.
@ref s 103(1) (src:2347)
GIVEN extent IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      date IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(1) the assessed extent of the disablement reaches the least extent` MEANS
    CONSIDER extent
    WHEN JUST e THEN JUST (e AT LEAST (`s 103(1) the least extent of disablement for a claim made on the date, as a percentage` date))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the assessment is made under Schedule 6, which is another part's

-- src:2347 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this section, an employed earner shall be entitled to disablement pension if he suffers as the result of the relevant accident from loss of physical or mental faculty such that the assessed extent of the resulting disablement amounts to not less than 14 per cent. or, on a claim made before 1st October 1986, 20 per cent.
@ref s 103(1) (src:2347)
GIVEN `s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person suffers as the result of the relevant accident from loss of physical or mental faculty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the date of the claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for "an employed earner"; for anyone else, or while it is unknown whether the person is one, no "if" below can be read as the text's no"
        IF NOT (`the person suffers as the result of the relevant accident from loss of physical or mental faculty`) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be entitled to disablement pension if he suffers as the result of the relevant accident from loss of physical or mental faculty"
        IF (`s 103(1) the assessed extent of the disablement reaches the least extent` `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage` `the date of the claim`) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... the assessed extent of the resulting disablement amounts to not less than 14 per cent. or, on a claim made before 1st October 1986, 20 per cent."
        IF (`s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND ((`s 103(1) the assessed extent of the disablement reaches the least extent` `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage` `the date of the claim`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an employed earner is section 2's answer, and the assessment is Schedule 6's

-- s 103(2): "there may be added to the percentage of the disablement resulting from the relevant accident the assessed percentage of any present disablement of his (a) which resulted from any other accident ... arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner's employment, and (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement,
-- (as well as any percentage which may be so added in accordance with regulations under subsection (2) of section 109 below made by virtue of subsection (4)(b) of that section)."
-- "May be added": the subsection permits the addition; it does not say that an earlier disablement outside (a) and (b) may not be added, so the permission function is NOTHING there. The aggregate function adds the permitted ones.
-- src:2348 | (2) In the determination of the extent of an employed earner’s disablement for the purposes of this section there may be added to the percentage of the disablement resulting from the relevant accident the assessed percentage of any present disablement of his—
-- src:2349 | (a) which resulted from any other accident ... arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner’s employment, and
-- src:2350 | (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement,
-- src:2351 | (as well as any percentage which may be so added in accordance with regulations under subsection (2) of section 109 below made by virtue of subsection (4)(b) of that section).
@ref s 103(2) (src:2348-2351)
DECLARE `s 103(2) Earlier disablement` HAS
    `the assessed percentage of the present disablement` IS A NUMBER
    `it resulted from another accident arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2348 | (2) In the determination of the extent of an employed earner’s disablement for the purposes of this section there may be added to the percentage of the disablement resulting from the relevant accident the assessed percentage of any present disablement of his—
-- src:2349 | (a) which resulted from any other accident ... arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner’s employment, and
-- src:2350 | (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement,
-- src:2351 | (as well as any percentage which may be so added in accordance with regulations under subsection (2) of section 109 below made by virtue of subsection (4)(b) of that section).
@ref s 103(2) (src:2348-2351)
GIVEN earlier IS A `s 103(2) Earlier disablement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(2) the earlier disablement may be added` MEANS
    IF   earlier's `it resulted from another accident arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner's employment` AND earlier's `a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "there may be added ... any present disablement of his (a) which resulted from any other accident ... and (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid"; the subsection does not say that others may not be added

-- src:2348 | (2) In the determination of the extent of an employed earner’s disablement for the purposes of this section there may be added to the percentage of the disablement resulting from the relevant accident the assessed percentage of any present disablement of his—
-- src:2349 | (a) which resulted from any other accident ... arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner’s employment, and
-- src:2350 | (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement,
-- src:2351 | (as well as any percentage which may be so added in accordance with regulations under subsection (2) of section 109 below made by virtue of subsection (4)(b) of that section).
@ref s 103(2) (src:2348-2351)
GIVEN `the percentage of the disablement resulting from the relevant accident` IS A NUMBER
      `the earlier disablements` IS A LIST OF `s 103(2) Earlier disablement`
      `s 109(2) the percentage added in accordance with regulations under section 109(2) made by virtue of section 109(4)(b)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 103(2) the aggregate percentage with every addition the subsection permits` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 109(2) the percentage added in accordance with regulations under section 109(2) made by virtue of section 109(4)(b)`
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (`the percentage of the disablement resulting from the relevant accident` PLUS (sum (map (GIVEN d YIELD d's `the assessed percentage of the present disablement`) (filter (GIVEN d YIELD (`s 103(2) the earlier disablement may be added` d) EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the earlier disablements`))) PLUS r)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the percentage added by regulations under section 109(2) is not supplied

-- s 103(3): "Subject to subsection (4) below, where the assessment of disablement is a percentage between 20 and 100 which is not a multiple of 10, it shall be treated (a) if it is a multiple of 5, as being the next higher percentage which is a multiple of 10, and (b) if it is not a multiple of 5, as being the nearest percentage which is a multiple of 10,
-- and where the assessment of disablement on a claim made on or after 1st October 1986 is less than 20 per cent., but not less than 14 per cent., it shall be treated as 20 per cent."
-- An assessment outside those cases stands as assessed (fork F11): "treated as" changes only the cases it names.
-- src:2352 | (3) Subject to subsection (4) below, where the assessment of disablement is a percentage between 20 and 100 which is not a multiple of 10, it shall be treated—
-- src:2353 | (a) if it is a multiple of 5, as being the next higher percentage which is a multiple of 10, and
-- src:2354 | (b) if it is not a multiple of 5, as being the nearest percentage which is a multiple of 10,
-- src:2355 | and where the assessment of disablement on a claim made on or after 1st October 1986 is less than 20 per cent., but not less than 14 per cent., it shall be treated as 20 per cent.
@ref s 103(3) (src:2352-2355)
GIVEN percentage IS A NUMBER
      date IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` MEANS
    IF   (percentage GREATER THAN 20) AND (percentage LESS THAN 100) AND (NOT ((percentage MODULO 10) EQUALS 0))
    THEN IF   (percentage MODULO 5) EQUALS 0
         THEN percentage PLUS 5    -- (a) a multiple of 5: "the next higher percentage which is a multiple of 10"
         ELSE IF   (percentage MODULO 10) LESS THAN 5
              THEN percentage MINUS (percentage MODULO 10)    -- (b) "the nearest percentage which is a multiple of 10", below
              ELSE percentage PLUS (10 MINUS (percentage MODULO 10))    -- (b) "the nearest percentage which is a multiple of 10", above
    ELSE IF   (date AT LEAST Date 1 10 1986) AND (percentage LESS THAN 20) AND (percentage AT LEAST 14)
         THEN 20    -- "on a claim made on or after 1st October 1986 is less than 20 per cent., but not less than 14 per cent., it shall be treated as 20 per cent."
         ELSE percentage    -- the assessment stands as assessed (fork F11); this is neither a FALSE nor a NOTHING

-- s 103(4): "Where subsection (2) above applies, subsection (3) above shall have effect in relation to the aggregate percentage and not in relation to any percentage forming part of the aggregate."
-- src:2356 | (4) Where subsection (2) above applies, subsection (3) above shall have effect in relation to the aggregate percentage and not in relation to any percentage forming part of the aggregate.
@ref s 103(4) (src:2356)
GIVEN `subsection (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the percentage of the disablement resulting from the relevant accident` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 103(4) the percentage to which subsection (3) applies` MEANS
    IF   `subsection (2) applies`
    THEN `the aggregate percentage`    -- "subsection (3) above shall have effect in relation to the aggregate percentage and not in relation to any percentage forming part of the aggregate"
    ELSE `the percentage of the disablement resulting from the relevant accident`    -- subsection (4) is for "Where subsection (2) above applies"; without it, the one assessment is what subsection (3) reads

-- s 103(5): "In this Part of this Act “assessed”, in relation to the extent of any disablement, means assessed in accordance with Schedule 6 to this Act;"
-- src:2357 | (5) In this Part of this Act “assessed”, in relation to the extent of any disablement, means assessed in accordance with Schedule 6 to this Act; and for the purposes of that Schedule there shall be taken to be no relevant loss of faculty when the extent of the resulting disablement, if so assessed, would not amount to 1 per cent.
@ref s 103(5) (src:2357)
GIVEN `the extent was assessed in accordance with Schedule 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(5) the extent of the disablement is assessed` MEANS
    IF   `the extent was assessed in accordance with Schedule 6`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“assessed” ... means assessed in accordance with Schedule 6 to this Act"

-- s 103(5), second limb: "for the purposes of that Schedule there shall be taken to be no relevant loss of faculty when the extent of the resulting disablement, if so assessed, would not amount to 1 per cent."
-- Below 1 per cent: taken to be no relevant loss. At 1 per cent or more the sentence is silent.
-- src:2357 | (5) In this Part of this Act “assessed”, in relation to the extent of any disablement, means assessed in accordance with Schedule 6 to this Act; and for the purposes of that Schedule there shall be taken to be no relevant loss of faculty when the extent of the resulting disablement, if so assessed, would not amount to 1 per cent.
@ref s 103(5) (src:2357)
GIVEN `sch 6 the extent of the disablement if so assessed, as a percentage` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(5) there is taken to be no relevant loss of faculty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 6 the extent of the disablement if so assessed, as a percentage`
    WHEN JUST e THEN IF e LESS THAN 1 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for the case where the extent "would not amount to 1 per cent."
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the assessment is Schedule 6's

-- s 103(6): "A person shall not be entitled to a disablement pension until after the expiry of the period of 90 days (disregarding Sundays) beginning with the day of the relevant accident."
-- The period is read as 90 days that are not Sundays, counted from the accident day (fork F13); the person is barred through the 90th such day and not barred from the day after it.
-- src:2358 | (6) A person shall not be entitled to a disablement pension until after the expiry of the period of 90 days (disregarding Sundays) beginning with the day of the relevant accident.
@ref s 103(6) (src:2358)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` MEANS
    IF   (`s 70(1A) the days since the last Sunday` day) EQUALS 0
    THEN `s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` (day PLUS 1) n
    ELSE IF   n AT MOST 1
         THEN day
         ELSE `s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` (day PLUS 1) (n MINUS 1)

-- src:2358 | (6) A person shall not be entitled to a disablement pension until after the expiry of the period of 90 days (disregarding Sundays) beginning with the day of the relevant accident.
@ref s 103(6) (src:2358)
GIVEN `the day of the relevant accident` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(6) the person is barred from a disablement pension for the day by the 90 days` MEANS
    IF   day AT MOST (`s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` `the day of the relevant accident` 90)
    THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no in its own words: "A person shall not be entitled to a disablement pension until after the expiry of the period of 90 days (disregarding Sundays) beginning with the day of the relevant accident"
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until after the expiry of the period"; after the expiry the bar does not run

-- s 103(7): "Subject to subsection (8) below, where disablement pension is payable for a period, it shall be paid at the appropriate weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 1."
-- src:2359 | (7) Subject to subsection (8) below, where disablement pension is payable for a period, it shall be paid at the appropriate weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 1.
@ref s 103(7) (src:2359)
GIVEN `the disablement pension is payable for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 4 pt V para 1 the appropriate weekly rate of disablement pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 103(7) the weekly rate at which the disablement pension is paid in pounds` MEANS
    IF   `the disablement pension is payable for the period`
    THEN `sch 4 pt V para 1 the appropriate weekly rate of disablement pension in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where disablement pension is payable for a period, it shall be paid at the appropriate weekly rate"; a period for which it is not payable is not addressed

-- s 103(8): "Where the period referred to in subsection (7) above is limited by reference to a definite date, the pension shall cease on the death of the beneficiary before that date."
-- src:2360 | (8) Where the period referred to in subsection (7) above is limited by reference to a definite date, the pension shall cease on the death of the beneficiary before that date.
@ref s 103(8) (src:2360)
GIVEN `the date by reference to which the period is limited` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date of the death of the beneficiary` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103(8) the pension ceases on the death of the beneficiary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date by reference to which the period is limited`
    WHEN JUST limit THEN
        CONSIDER `the date of the death of the beneficiary`
        WHEN JUST death THEN IF death LESS THAN limit THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for a death "before that date"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): no date of death is given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for a period "limited by reference to a definite date"

§§ `s 104 -- Increase where constant attendance needed`

-- s 104(1): "Where a disablement pension is payable in respect of an assessment of 100 per cent., then, if as the result of the relevant loss of faculty the beneficiary requires constant attendance, the weekly rate of the pension shall be increased"
-- src:2362 | (1) Where a disablement pension is payable in respect of an assessment of 100 per cent., then, if as the result of the relevant loss of faculty the beneficiary requires constant attendance, the weekly rate of the pension shall be increased by an amount, not exceeding the appropriate amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2 determined in accordance with regulations by reference to the extent and nature of the attendance required by the beneficiary.
@ref s 104(1) (src:2362)
GIVEN `the disablement pension is payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment in respect of which the pension is payable, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER
      `as the result of the relevant loss of faculty the beneficiary requires constant attendance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 104(1) the weekly rate of the pension is increased for constant attendance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the disablement pension is payable` AND (`the assessment in respect of which the pension is payable, as a percentage` EQUALS 100)) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is for "a disablement pension ... payable in respect of an assessment of 100 per cent."
        IF NOT (`as the result of the relevant loss of faculty the beneficiary requires constant attendance`) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then, if as the result of the relevant loss of faculty the beneficiary requires constant attendance, the weekly rate of the pension shall be increased"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 104(1): "by an amount, not exceeding the appropriate amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2 determined in accordance with regulations by reference to the extent and nature of the attendance required by the beneficiary."
-- The amount the regulations determine is an input; if it would exceed the Schedule 4 figure the figure is the most the subsection allows (fork F12).
-- src:2362 | (1) Where a disablement pension is payable in respect of an assessment of 100 per cent., then, if as the result of the relevant loss of faculty the beneficiary requires constant attendance, the weekly rate of the pension shall be increased by an amount, not exceeding the appropriate amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2 determined in accordance with regulations by reference to the extent and nature of the attendance required by the beneficiary.
@ref s 104(1) (src:2362)
GIVEN `the increase applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount determined in accordance with regulations by reference to the extent and nature of the attendance required in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt V para 2 the appropriate amount in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 104(1) the amount of the increase in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the increase applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `the amount determined in accordance with regulations by reference to the extent and nature of the attendance required in pounds`
        WHEN JUST determined THEN
            CONSIDER `sch 4 pt V para 2 the appropriate amount in pounds`
            WHEN JUST cap THEN IF determined AT MOST cap THEN JUST determined ELSE JUST cap    -- "not exceeding the appropriate amount"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the amount is determined in accordance with regulations
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no increase under subsection (1) has an amount
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the increase applies is not supplied

-- s 104(2): "An increase of pension under this section shall be payable for such period as may be determined at the time it is granted, but may be renewed from time to time."
-- The deciding officer fixes the period; what the subsection means for the person is that the increase is payable on the days of that period. Outside it the subsection does not say no: it may be renewed.
-- src:2363 | (2) An increase of pension under this section shall be payable for such period as may be determined at the time it is granted, but may be renewed from time to time.
@ref s 104(2) (src:2363)
GIVEN `the period determined when the increase was granted` IS A Period
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 104(2) the increase is payable on the day` MEANS
    IF   (day AT LEAST (`the period determined when the increase was granted`'s `the first day`)) AND (day AT MOST (`the period determined when the increase was granted`'s `the last day`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be payable for such period as may be determined at the time it is granted, but may be renewed from time to time"; a day outside the period is not decided, and a renewal may cover it
-- s 104(3): regulations may direct that ss 64 to 67 have effect in relation to the increases (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).

-- s 104(4): "In subsection (3) above, “modifications” includes additions and omissions."
-- src:2365 | (4) In subsection (3) above, “modifications” includes additions and omissions.
@ref s 104(4) (src:2365)
GIVEN `the change is an addition or an omission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 104(4) the change is a modification` MEANS
    IF   `the change is an addition or an omission`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“modifications” includes additions and omissions"; other changes are not stated to be outside the word

§§ `s 105 -- Increase for exceptionally severe disablement`

-- s 105(1): "Where a disablement pension is payable to a person (a) who is or, but for having received medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution, would be entitled to an increase of the weekly rate of the pension under section 104 above, and the weekly rate of the increase exceeds the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2(a); and
-- (b) his need for constant attendance of an extent and nature qualifying him for such an increase at a weekly rate in excess of that amount is likely to be permanent, the weekly rate of the pension shall, in addition to any increase under section 104 above, be further increased by the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 3."
-- "Where" with no "if": a case in which the increase is made; failure is NOTHING (fork F7).
-- src:2367 | (1) Where a disablement pension is payable to a person—
-- src:2368 | (a) who is or, but for having received medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution, would be entitled to an increase of the weekly rate of the pension under section 104 above, and the weekly rate of the increase exceeds the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2(a); and
-- src:2369 | (b) his need for constant attendance of an extent and nature qualifying him for such an increase at a weekly rate in excess of that amount is likely to be permanent,
-- src:2370 | the weekly rate of the pension shall, in addition to any increase under section 104 above, be further increased by the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 3.
@ref s 105(1) (src:2367-2370)
GIVEN `the disablement pension is payable to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is, or but for having received medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution would be, entitled to an increase under section 104` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of the increase under section 104 in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt V para 2(a) the amount specified in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `his need for constant attendance of an extent and nature qualifying him for such an increase at a weekly rate in excess of that amount is likely to be permanent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(1) the weekly rate of the pension is further increased` MEANS
    IF   `the disablement pension is payable to the person`
         AND (`the person is, or but for having received medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution would be, entitled to an increase under section 104` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND (`s 105(1) the weekly rate of the increase exceeds the amount` `the weekly rate of the increase under section 104 in pounds` `sch 4 pt V para 2(a) the amount specified in pounds` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND `his need for constant attendance of an extent and nature qualifying him for such an increase at a weekly rate in excess of that amount is likely to be permanent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a disablement pension is payable to a person (a) ... and (b) ..., the weekly rate of the pension shall ... be further increased"; a case outside is not addressed

-- s 105(1)(a), the comparison: "the weekly rate of the increase exceeds the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2(a)".
-- src:2368 | (a) who is or, but for having received medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution, would be entitled to an increase of the weekly rate of the pension under section 104 above, and the weekly rate of the increase exceeds the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2(a); and
@ref s 105(1)(a) (src:2368)
GIVEN rate IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      amount IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(1) the weekly rate of the increase exceeds the amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER rate
    WHEN JUST r THEN
        CONSIDER amount
        WHEN JUST a THEN JUST (r GREATER THAN a)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the rate of the increase under section 104 is not supplied

-- s 105(1): the amount of the further increase is "the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 3".
-- src:2370 | the weekly rate of the pension shall, in addition to any increase under section 104 above, be further increased by the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 3.
@ref s 105(1) (src:2370)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the pension is further increased` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 4 pt V para 3 the amount specified in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 105(1) the amount of the further increase in pounds` MEANS
    IF   `the weekly rate of the pension is further increased` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN `sch 4 pt V para 3 the amount specified in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amount is for the case in which the weekly rate "shall ... be further increased"

-- s 105(2): "An increase under this section shall be payable for such period as may be determined at the time it is granted, but may be renewed from time to time." Read as section 104(2).
-- src:2371 | (2) An increase under this section shall be payable for such period as may be determined at the time it is granted, but may be renewed from time to time.
@ref s 105(2) (src:2371)
GIVEN `the period determined when the increase was granted` IS A Period
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(2) the increase is payable on the day` MEANS
    IF   (day AT LEAST (`the period determined when the increase was granted`'s `the first day`)) AND (day AT MOST (`the period determined when the increase was granted`'s `the last day`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be payable for such period as may be determined at the time it is granted, but may be renewed from time to time"; a day outside the period is not decided, and a renewal may cover it

§§ `s 106 -- Benefits and increases subject to qualifications as to time`

-- s 106: "Schedule 7 to this Act shall have effect in relation (a) to unemployability supplement; (b) to disablement gratuity; (c) to increases of disablement pension during hospital treatment; (d) to reduced earnings allowance; (e) to retirement allowance; and (f) to industrial death benefit,
-- for all of which the qualifications include special qualifications as to time."
-- The core's Benefit lacks disablement gratuity and the hospital-treatment increases, so this section has its own type.
-- src:2374 | Schedule 7 to this Act shall have effect in relation—
-- src:2375 | (a) to unemployability supplement;
-- src:2376 | (b) to disablement gratuity;
-- src:2377 | (c) to increases of disablement pension during hospital treatment;
-- src:2378 | (d) to reduced earnings allowance;
-- src:2379 | (e) to retirement allowance; and
-- src:2380 | (f) to industrial death benefit,
-- src:2381 | for all of which the qualifications include special qualifications as to time.
@ref s 106 (src:2374-2381)
DECLARE `s 106 Benefit or increase` IS ONE OF
    `s 106(a) unemployability supplement`
    `s 106(b) disablement gratuity`
    `s 106(c) an increase of disablement pension during hospital treatment`
    `s 106(d) reduced earnings allowance`
    `s 106(e) retirement allowance`
    `s 106(f) industrial death benefit`
    `s 106 another benefit or increase`

-- src:2374 | Schedule 7 to this Act shall have effect in relation—
-- src:2375 | (a) to unemployability supplement;
-- src:2376 | (b) to disablement gratuity;
-- src:2377 | (c) to increases of disablement pension during hospital treatment;
-- src:2378 | (d) to reduced earnings allowance;
-- src:2379 | (e) to retirement allowance; and
-- src:2380 | (f) to industrial death benefit,
-- src:2381 | for all of which the qualifications include special qualifications as to time.
@ref s 106 (src:2374-2381)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 106 Benefit or increase`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106 Schedule 7 has effect in relation to the benefit or increase` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 106(a) unemployability supplement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 106(b) disablement gratuity` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 106(c) an increase of disablement pension during hospital treatment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 106(d) reduced earnings allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 106(e) retirement allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 106(f) industrial death benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Schedule 7 to this Act shall have effect in relation" to these six; the section does not say that it has no effect in relation to others

§§ `s 107 -- Adjustments for successive accidents`

-- s 107(2): "The increases of benefit referred to in subsection (1) above are those under the following provisions of this Act: section 104, section 105, paragraph 2, 4 or 6 of Schedule 7." The list is closed.
-- src:2389 | (2) The increases of benefit referred to in subsection (1) above are those under the following provisions of this Act—
-- src:2390 | section 104,
-- src:2391 | section 105,
-- src:2392 | paragraph 2, 4 or 6 of Schedule 7.
@ref s 107(2) (src:2389-2392)
DECLARE `s 107(2) Provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 107(2) section 104`
    `s 107(2) section 105`
    `s 107(2) paragraph 2 of Schedule 7`
    `s 107(2) paragraph 4 of Schedule 7`
    `s 107(2) paragraph 6 of Schedule 7`
    `s 107(2) another provision`

-- src:2389 | (2) The increases of benefit referred to in subsection (1) above are those under the following provisions of this Act—
-- src:2390 | section 104,
-- src:2391 | section 105,
-- src:2392 | paragraph 2, 4 or 6 of Schedule 7.
@ref s 107(2) (src:2389-2392)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 107(2) Provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(2) the increase is one referred to in subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 107(2) section 104` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 107(2) section 105` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 107(2) paragraph 2 of Schedule 7` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 107(2) paragraph 4 of Schedule 7` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 107(2) paragraph 6 of Schedule 7` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The increases of benefit referred to in subsection (1) above are those under the following provisions of this Act"

-- s 107(1)(a): "Where a person suffers two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of his employed earner's employment (a) he shall not for the same period be entitled (apart from any increase of benefit mentioned in subsection (2) below) to receive industrial injuries benefit by way of two or more disablement pensions at an aggregate weekly rate exceeding the appropriate amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 4;"
-- The aggregate is taken apart from the increases in subsection (2). The bar is a flat negative limited by "exceeding".
-- src:2384 | (1) Where a person suffers two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of his employed earner’s employment—
-- src:2385 | (a) he shall not for the same period be entitled (apart from any increase of benefit mentioned in subsection (2) below) to receive industrial injuries benefit by way of two or more disablement pensions at an aggregate weekly rate exceeding the appropriate amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 4; and
@ref s 107(1)(a) (src:2384-2385)
GIVEN `the person suffers two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of his employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate weekly rate of the disablement pensions for the same period, apart from any increase mentioned in subsection (2), in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt V para 4 the appropriate amount in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(1)(a) the person is barred from an aggregate weekly rate above the appropriate amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person suffers two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of his employed earner's employment`) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for "a person [who] suffers two or more successive accidents"
        IF `sch 4 pt V para 4 the appropriate amount in pounds` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied
        IF `sch 4 pt V para 4 the appropriate amount in pounds` EQUALS JUST `the aggregate weekly rate of the disablement pensions for the same period, apart from any increase mentioned in subsection (2), in pounds` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for a rate "exceeding the appropriate amount"; a rate equal to it does not exceed it
        OTHERWISE `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate rate exceeds the appropriate amount` `the aggregate weekly rate of the disablement pensions for the same period, apart from any increase mentioned in subsection (2), in pounds` `sch 4 pt V para 4 the appropriate amount in pounds`

-- src:2384 | (1) Where a person suffers two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of his employed earner’s employment—
-- src:2385 | (a) he shall not for the same period be entitled (apart from any increase of benefit mentioned in subsection (2) below) to receive industrial injuries benefit by way of two or more disablement pensions at an aggregate weekly rate exceeding the appropriate amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 4; and
@ref s 107(1)(a) (src:2384-2385)
GIVEN aggregate IS A NUMBER
      amount IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(1)(a) the aggregate rate exceeds the appropriate amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER amount
    WHEN JUST a THEN IF aggregate GREATER THAN a THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "shall not for the same period be entitled ... to receive ... at an aggregate weekly rate exceeding the appropriate amount"; NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) for a rate that does not exceed it
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied

-- s 107(1)(a): the most the person may receive for the same period, apart from the increases, is the appropriate amount.
-- src:2384 | (1) Where a person suffers two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of his employed earner’s employment—
-- src:2385 | (a) he shall not for the same period be entitled (apart from any increase of benefit mentioned in subsection (2) below) to receive industrial injuries benefit by way of two or more disablement pensions at an aggregate weekly rate exceeding the appropriate amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 4; and
@ref s 107(1)(a) (src:2384-2385)
GIVEN `the person suffers two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of his employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate weekly rate of the disablement pensions for the same period, apart from any increase mentioned in subsection (2), in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt V para 4 the appropriate amount in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 107(1)(a) the aggregate weekly rate the person may receive for the same period, apart from increases, in pounds` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`the person suffers two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of his employed earner's employment`)
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for a person who "suffers two or more successive accidents"
    ELSE CONSIDER `sch 4 pt V para 4 the appropriate amount in pounds`
         WHEN JUST a THEN IF `the aggregate weekly rate of the disablement pensions for the same period, apart from any increase mentioned in subsection (2), in pounds` GREATER THAN a THEN JUST a ELSE JUST `the aggregate weekly rate of the disablement pensions for the same period, apart from any increase mentioned in subsection (2), in pounds`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied

-- s 107(1)(b): regulations may provide for adjusting disablement benefit and the increases in subsection (2) (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).

§§ `s 108 -- Benefit in respect of prescribed industrial diseases, etc.`

-- s 108(1): "Industrial injuries benefits shall, in respect of a person who has been in employed earner's employment, be payable in accordance with this section and sections 109 and 110 below in respect of (a) any prescribed disease, or (b) any prescribed personal injury (other than an injury caused by accident arising out of and in the course of his employment), which is a disease or injury due to the nature of that employment ...."
-- "Shall ... be payable": a case in which the benefits are payable. Failure is NOTHING (fork F7).
-- src:2395 | (1) Industrial injuries benefits shall, in respect of a person who has been in employed earner’s employment, be payable in accordance with this section and sections 109 and 110 below in respect of—
-- src:2396 | (a) any prescribed disease, or
-- src:2397 | (b) any prescribed personal injury (other than an injury caused by accident arising out of and in the course of his employment),
-- src:2398 | which is a disease or injury due to the nature of that employment ....
@ref s 108(1) (src:2395-2398)
GIVEN `the person has been in employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disease is a prescribed disease` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the personal injury is a prescribed personal injury` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the injury was caused by accident arising out of and in the course of his employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disease or injury is due to the nature of that employment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(1) industrial injuries benefits are payable in respect of the prescribed disease or injury` MEANS
    IF   `the person has been in employed earner's employment`
         AND (`the disease or injury is due to the nature of that employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND ((`the disease is a prescribed disease` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
              OR ((`the personal injury is a prescribed personal injury` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (NOT (`the injury was caused by accident arising out of and in the course of his employment`))))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Industrial injuries benefits shall ... be payable ... in respect of" these; the subsection does not say that they are payable only there, and what is prescribed is for regulations outside the sources

-- s 108(2): a disease or injury may be prescribed if the Secretary of State is satisfied of (a) and (b) (a condition on the making of regulations; inert, machinery).
-- s 108(3): regulations may treat a person as if the regulations had been in force earlier (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).
-- s 108(4): provision may be made by regulations for the time of development and recrudescence (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).
-- s 108(5): the power in subsection (4)(a) includes the date of first claim (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).

-- s 108(6): "a person shall not be entitled to benefit in respect of a disease as being an injury by accident arising out of and in the course of any employment if at the time of the accident the disease is in relation to him a prescribed disease by virtue of the occupation in which he is engaged in that employment."
-- The opening words, "Nothing in this section or in section 109 or 110 below affects the right of any person to benefit in respect of a disease which is a personal injury by accident", preserve the right and give no rule of their own; the exception is the rule.
-- src:2407 | (6) Nothing in this section or in section 109 or 110 below affects the right of any person to benefit in respect of a disease which is a personal injury by accident within the meaning of this Part of this Act, except that a person shall not be entitled to benefit in respect of a disease as being an injury by accident arising out of and in the course of any employment if at the time of the accident the disease is in relation to him a prescribed disease by virtue of the occupation in which he is engaged in that employment.
@ref s 108(6) (src:2407)
GIVEN `the person claims benefit in respect of a disease as being an injury by accident arising out of and in the course of an employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the accident the disease is in relation to him a prescribed disease by virtue of the occupation in which he is engaged in that employment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(6) the person is barred from benefit in respect of a disease as an injury by accident` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person claims benefit in respect of a disease as being an injury by accident arising out of and in the course of an employment`) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception is for "benefit in respect of a disease as being an injury by accident arising out of and in the course of any employment"
        IF `at the time of the accident the disease is in relation to him a prescribed disease by virtue of the occupation in which he is engaged in that employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "a person shall not be entitled to benefit in respect of a disease as being an injury by accident ... if at the time of the accident the disease is in relation to him a prescribed disease by virtue of the occupation"
        IF `at the time of the accident the disease is in relation to him a prescribed disease by virtue of the occupation in which he is engaged in that employment` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled ... if at the time of the accident the disease is in relation to him a prescribed disease by virtue of the occupation" does not apply when it is not
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the disease is prescribed by virtue of the occupation is for regulations outside the sources

§§ `s 109 -- General provisions relating to benefit under section 108`

-- s 109(1): "Subject to the power to make different provision by regulations, and to the following provisions of this section and section 110 below (a) the benefit payable under section 108 above in respect of a prescribed disease or injury, and (b) the conditions for receipt of benefit, shall be the same as in the case of personal injury by accident arising out of and in the course of employment."
-- src:2409 | (1) Subject to the power to make different provision by regulations, and to the following provisions of this section and section 110 below—
-- src:2410 | (a) the benefit payable under section 108 above in respect of a prescribed disease or injury, and
-- src:2411 | (b) the conditions for receipt of benefit,
-- src:2412 | shall be the same as in the case of personal injury by accident arising out of and in the course of employment.
@ref s 109(1) (src:2409-2412)
GIVEN `different provision is made by regulations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a following provision of this section or of section 110 provides otherwise` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1) the benefit and the conditions for receipt are the same as for personal injury by accident` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`different provision is made by regulations` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`a following provision of this section or of section 110 provides otherwise` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to the power to make different provision by regulations, and to the following provisions of this section and section 110 below"
        IF (`different provision is made by regulations` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`a following provision of this section or of section 110 provides otherwise` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations or a later provision make different provision is not supplied

-- s 109(2): in relation to prescribed diseases and injuries, regulations may modify provisions and adapt references to accidents (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).
-- s 109(2), last words: "for the purposes of this subsection the provisions of that Act and that Chapter which relate to the administration of disablement benefit or reduced earnings allowance shall be taken to include section 1 of that Act and any provision which relates to the administration of both the benefit in question and other benefits."
-- src:2416 | and for the purposes of this subsection the provisions of that Act and that Chapter which relate to the administration of disablement benefit or reduced earnings allowance shall be taken to include section 1 of that Act and any provision which relates to the administration of both the benefit in question and other benefits.
@ref s 109(2) (src:2416)
GIVEN `the provision is section 1 of the Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision relates to the administration of both the benefit in question and other benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(2) the provision is taken to relate to the administration of disablement benefit or reduced earnings allowance` MEANS
    IF   `the provision is section 1 of the Administration Act` OR `the provision relates to the administration of both the benefit in question and other benefits`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "shall be taken to include" these; other provisions are decided by the ordinary meaning of "relate to", which is outside the text

-- s 109(3): regulations under subsection (2) may in particular include presumptions and incidental provision (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).
-- s 109(4): regulations under subsection (2) may also provide for adding the appropriate percentage (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).

-- s 109(5): in subsection (4)(a) "the appropriate percentage" means the assessed percentage of any present disablement of the earner which resulted (a) from any accident arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner's employment, or (b) from any other prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of that employment,
-- "and in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement."
-- src:2425 | (5) In subsection (4)(a) above “the appropriate percentage” means the assessed percentage of any present disablement of the earner which resulted—
-- src:2426 | (a) from any accident ... arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner’s employment, or
-- src:2427 | (b) from any other prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of that employment ... ,
-- src:2428 | and in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement.
@ref s 109(5) (src:2425-2428)
DECLARE `s 109(5) Present disablement` HAS
    `the assessed percentage` IS A NUMBER
    `it resulted from an accident arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it resulted from another prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2425 | (5) In subsection (4)(a) above “the appropriate percentage” means the assessed percentage of any present disablement of the earner which resulted—
-- src:2426 | (a) from any accident ... arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner’s employment, or
-- src:2427 | (b) from any other prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of that employment ... ,
-- src:2428 | and in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement.
@ref s 109(5) (src:2425-2428)
GIVEN disablement IS A `s 109(5) Present disablement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(5) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` MEANS
    IF   (disablement's `it resulted from an accident arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner's employment` OR disablement's `it resulted from another prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of that employment`)
         AND disablement's `a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the appropriate percentage” means the assessed percentage of any present disablement of the earner which resulted ... and in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid"

-- s 109(6): in subsection (4)(b) "the appropriate percentage" means the assessed percentage of any present disablement of the earner (a) which resulted from any prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of his employment, and (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement.
-- src:2429 | (6) In subsection (4)(b) above “the appropriate percentage” means the assessed percentage of any present disablement of the earner—
-- src:2430 | (a) which resulted from any prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of his employment ... , and
-- src:2431 | (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement.
@ref s 109(6) (src:2429-2431)
DECLARE `s 109(6) Present disablement` HAS
    `the assessed percentage` IS A NUMBER
    `it resulted from a prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of his employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2429 | (6) In subsection (4)(b) above “the appropriate percentage” means the assessed percentage of any present disablement of the earner—
-- src:2430 | (a) which resulted from any prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of his employment ... , and
-- src:2431 | (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement.
@ref s 109(6) (src:2429-2431)
GIVEN disablement IS A `s 109(6) Present disablement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(6) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` MEANS
    IF   disablement's `it resulted from a prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of his employment` AND disablement's `a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the appropriate percentage” means the assessed percentage of any present disablement of the earner (a) which resulted from any prescribed disease or injury ... and (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid"

-- src:2425 | (5) In subsection (4)(a) above “the appropriate percentage” means the assessed percentage of any present disablement of the earner which resulted—
-- src:2426 | (a) from any accident ... arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner’s employment, or
-- src:2427 | (b) from any other prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of that employment ... ,
-- src:2428 | and in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement.
-- src:2429 | (6) In subsection (4)(b) above “the appropriate percentage” means the assessed percentage of any present disablement of the earner—
-- src:2430 | (a) which resulted from any prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of his employment ... , and
-- src:2431 | (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement.
@ref s 109(5), s 109(6) (src:2425-2431)
GIVEN disablements IS A LIST OF `s 109(5) Present disablement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 109(5) the appropriate percentage for subsection (4)(a)` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN d YIELD d's `the assessed percentage`) (filter (GIVEN d YIELD (`s 109(5) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` d) EQUALS JUST TRUE) disablements))

-- src:2429 | (6) In subsection (4)(b) above “the appropriate percentage” means the assessed percentage of any present disablement of the earner—
-- src:2430 | (a) which resulted from any prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of his employment ... , and
-- src:2431 | (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement.
@ref s 109(6) (src:2429-2431)
GIVEN disablements IS A LIST OF `s 109(6) Present disablement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 109(6) the appropriate percentage for subsection (4)(b)` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN d YIELD d's `the assessed percentage`) (filter (GIVEN d YIELD (`s 109(6) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` d) EQUALS JUST TRUE) disablements))

-- s 109(7): regulations under subsection (2) may provide that the corresponding provisions have effect in relation to the aggregate percentage (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).

§§ `s 110 -- Respiratory diseases`

-- s 110(1): as respects pneumoconiosis, regulations may further provide that the effects of tuberculosis are treated as effects of the pneumoconiosis (a regulation-making power; inert, machinery).
-- s 110(2): subsection (1) has effect as if "emphysema or chronic bronchitis" were inserted, but only for a person whose disablement would be assessed at not less than 50 per cent. (a limit on the regulation-making power in subsection (1); inert, machinery).

-- s 110(3): "A person found to be suffering from pneumoconiosis shall be treated for the purposes of this Act as suffering from a loss of faculty such that the assessed extent of the resulting disablement amounts to not less than 1 per cent."
-- src:2439 | (3) A person found to be suffering from pneumoconiosis shall be treated for the purposes of this Act as suffering from a loss of faculty such that the assessed extent of the resulting disablement amounts to not less than 1 per cent.
@ref s 110(3) (src:2439)
GIVEN `the person is found to be suffering from pneumoconiosis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 110(3) the least assessed extent of the disablement treated as resulting, as a percentage` MEANS
    IF   `the person is found to be suffering from pneumoconiosis`
    THEN JUST 1
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for "A person found to be suffering from pneumoconiosis"

-- s 110(4): "In respect of byssinosis, a person shall not (unless regulations otherwise provide) be entitled to disablement benefit unless he is found to be suffering, as the result of byssinosis, from loss of faculty which is likely to be permanent."
-- src:2440 | (4) In respect of byssinosis, a person shall not (unless regulations otherwise provide) be entitled to disablement benefit unless he is found to be suffering, as the result of byssinosis, from loss of faculty which is likely to be permanent.
@ref s 110(4) (src:2440)
GIVEN `the claim is in respect of byssinosis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations otherwise provide` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `he is found to be suffering, as the result of byssinosis, from loss of faculty which is likely to be permanent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(4) the person is barred from disablement benefit in respect of byssinosis` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the claim is in respect of byssinosis`) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for "In respect of byssinosis"
        IF `regulations otherwise provide` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(unless regulations otherwise provide)"
        IF `he is found to be suffering, as the result of byssinosis, from loss of faculty which is likely to be permanent` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not ... be entitled to disablement benefit unless he is found to be suffering, as the result of byssinosis, from loss of faculty which is likely to be permanent"
        IF `regulations otherwise provide` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "a person shall not (unless regulations otherwise provide) be entitled to disablement benefit unless he is found to be suffering, as the result of byssinosis, from loss of faculty which is likely to be permanent"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations otherwise provide is not supplied
